patients is highest when there is an initial
symptom improvement brought about by
treatment. In this period, the depressed patient
is out of the low mood and apathetic and more
likely to act on a Suicide plan. However,
admitted patients are monitored and cared for
during their stay. The risk of suicide is lower
compared to after discharge when the patient is
more likely to feel left on their own and there is
no ongoing support or monitoring.
Reference(s) +* Medscape - Early Postdischarge P
eriod Linked to Very High Suicide
Risk
* CHIR - Are Patients With Depressi
on at Heightened Risk of Suicide a
