bipolar disorder with psychotic features
presents to you, complaining of decreased
mood and appetite for the past two weeks. On
examination, you notice that he does not talk
much and only answers your questions briefly.
He seems to have decreased concentration and
avoid eye contact. He, however, denies
hallucinations and paranoid ideation. He Is
currently on olanzapine, which he has been
taking for the past two years. Which of the
following is the most appropriate initial
