consultation. They met six months ago and
have decided to move in and live together. Li
has a dog and loves it very much, but Janet is
severely afraid of dogs. She says, "I try to
overcome my fear, but even speaking of dogs
makes me panic." She says that when she was
a child, she was bitten by a dog and has been
afraid of them her whole life. They ask for
advice as to how to overcome her fear. Which
one of the following is the most appropriate
advice she should follow as the first step in
overcoming her fear of dogs?','{"A":"She should keep a picture of a dog in\nher diary.","B":"she should keep a picture of a dog in\nher room and at sight.","C":"She should learn and perform\nrelaxation techniques.","D":"She should try to imagine petting a\ndog.","E":"i Shesoula Da cxeDOoeed to doas to"}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 Psychiatry  (1).pdf","supporting_pages":[],"source_qid":null,"duplicate_group_id":"exact-25772161115d","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"9f152c9e412eab1611df","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 Psychiatry  (1).pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 Psychiatry  (1).pdf","source_page":146,"source_qid":null},{"record_id":"ec9fe256cd024964245b","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"Psychiatry  Amedex 2025.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Psychiatry  Amedex 2025.pdf","source_page":41,"source_qid":null}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"five_block_inferred","text_method":"tesseract_retry_200dpi_psm3","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'needs_verification','[]','low','{"record_id":"9f152c9e412eab1611df","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 Psychiatry  (1).pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 Psychiatry  (1).pdf","source_year":2025,"source_page":146,"source_qid":null,"domain_hint":"Mental Health","stem":"Janet and Li present to your practice for\nconsultation. They met six months ago and\nhave decided to move in and live together. Li\nhas a dog and loves it very much, but Janet is\nseverely afraid of dogs. She says, \"I try to\novercome my fear, but even speaking of dogs\nmakes me panic.\" She says that when she was\na child, she was bitten by a dog and has been\nafraid of them her whole life. They ask for\nadvice as to how to overcome her fear. Which\none of the following is the most appropriate\nadvice she should follow as the first step in\noverco