with complaints of anorexia, weight loss, loss of
interest in daily life, and a depressed mood for
the past three weeks. Evaluation reveals the
diagnosis to be major depression. You advise
that she take antidepressants as well as non-
pharmacological therapy, but she refuses to be
treated. Which one of the following would be
